      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: don't care if it causes issue in some worlds, it keeps it's setting between every world as i want it to, it only resets when i relaunch the game.  They added the dynamic setting to avoid the issue in most cases.  If there is visual issues with the skybox or something i can disable it myself if it's bad enough.\nMore often than not, more well thought-out world development can avoid clipping plane issues.  Most of the problems i've seen are easily be fixed by changing the approach.  Using shader fog instead of unity fog is one such example. (their example in the 3rd blog of test pilots is complete hogwash, cuz i used 0.01 clipping plane in that world since forever and it rendered just fine to my memory) Only cases i'd seen issue was when worlds made jank use of mesh skyboxes that were too close to the farplane instead of view-pos cubemap shaders for it, emulating unity internal skybox behaviour.\nHaving to set it again every launch is just another tedious step, and i often forget until i realize something is wrong with things going near my face and am vocally going \"ugh\" because i need to set it again.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
